-- EXPECT-ERROR: refinement violation
--
-- `@[trusted]` does NOT rescue a definite violation (§`@[trusted] — a scoped,
-- loud escape hatch`, 2026-07-30). This is the load-bearing limit stated
-- alongside the feature: `@[trusted]` accepts an obligation the checker could
-- not DECIDE (a skip) as an assertion, but a predicate the solver has
-- PROVED can never hold is a bug in the annotation, not an incompleteness to
-- wave through. Rescuing it would turn `@[trusted]` into a way to ship a
-- known-false contract, silently, inside a capability whose entire premise
-- is "these contracts are a guarantee, not a best effort".
--
-- `inner` demands `_ > 0`. `go` is annotated `@[trusted]` and calls
-- `inner(0 - 5)`, which the solver can definitely refute: this is reported
-- exactly as it would be with `@[trusted]` removed. Accept companion
-- `accept/t132_refine_trusted_rescues_cap_verified` is the case
-- `@[trusted]` DOES help -- an undischargeable SKIP, not a violation.
--
-- See specs/lang/refinement-types.md, "`@[trusted]` — a scoped, loud escape
-- hatch".
mod T133 do

  cap verified

  fn inner(n : {Int | _ > 0}) : Int do
    n
  end

  @[trusted]
  fn go() : Int do
    inner(0 - 5)
  end

  fn main() : Int do
    go()
  end

end
